---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  AccordionHero,
  AccordionVariants,
  AccordionCalendarFilters,
  AccordionImportSettings,
  AccordionRecoverProposal,
  AccordionAboutIntegration,
} from "../../components/AccordionDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Accordion"
  description="Stack sections of details, filters, and settings that open in place."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Accordion</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A stack of sections that open in place. Use it for filters, settings, and
    background details that most people do not need every time.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="accordion-demo"><AccordionHero client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Accordion usage"
      code={`import {
  Accordion,
  AccordionContent,
  AccordionItem,
  AccordionTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/accordion";

<Accordion multiple defaultValue={["one"]}>
  <AccordionItem value="one">
    <AccordionTrigger>What is this example?</AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>Real shared components with sample data.</AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
  <AccordionItem value="three" disabled>
    <AccordionTrigger>Disabled item</AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>Unavailable</AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
</Accordion>`}
    />
    <p>
      One section opens at a time. Pass <code>multiple</code> to let several stay
      open. Give items a <code>value</code> to open them with <code
        >defaultValue</code
      >, or control them with <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code>.
      An item without a value gets one of its own. <code>disabled</code> on an item
      blocks its trigger.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Trigger variants</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Trigger variants"
      code={`<AccordionTrigger>About this integration</AccordionTrigger>

<AccordionTrigger
  variant="quiet"
  aria-label="Google calendars"
  aria-describedby="source-summary"
>
  <span className="grid gap-1">
    <span>Google calendars</span>
    <span id="source-summary" className="text-xs font-normal">2 of 3 shown</span>
  </span>
</AccordionTrigger>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>default</code> underlines its label on hover. <code>quiet</code> does
      not, so a title with a summary line below it stays calm. Name a two-line trigger
      with <code>aria-label</code> and link the summary with <code
        >aria-describedby</code
      >.
    </p>
    <AccordionVariants client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="calendar-filters">
    <h2 class="section-title">Filters</h2>
    <p>
      In a filter rail, use <code>multiple</code> and <code>quiet</code> triggers
      whose summaries show the current choice while the section is closed.
    </p>
    <AccordionCalendarFilters client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Controlled settings</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Controlled accordion"
      code={`<Accordion
  value={open ? ["settings"] : []}
  onValueChange={(value) => setOpen(value.includes("settings"))}
>
  <AccordionItem value="settings">
    <AccordionTrigger>Import settings</AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>…</AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
</Accordion>
{!open && <p>Documentation, Issues · since Apr 1, 2026 · only you</p>}`}
    />
    <AccordionImportSettings client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="about-this-integration">
    <h2 class="section-title">Forms and details</h2>
    <p>
      A single section can hold a form, with its own loading and error feedback,
      or a few paragraphs of background. Paragraphs inside content are spaced,
      and links are underlined.
    </p>
    <AccordionRecoverProposal client:load />
    <AccordionAboutIntegration client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="accordion-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      The four parts wrap Base UI Accordion. Every Base UI prop works, including
      <code>multiple</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>defaultValue</code>,
      <code>onValueChange</code>, <code>disabled</code>, <code
        >hiddenUntilFound</code
      >, and <code>keepMounted</code>.
      <code>AccordionTrigger</code> adds <code>variant</code>; <code
        >accordionTriggerVariantNames</code
      > lists them. <code>className</code> on <code>AccordionContent</code> styles
      its padded inner box.
    </p>
    <p>
      Parts get <code>data-slot</code> values of <code>accordion</code>, <code
        >accordion-item</code
      >, <code>accordion-header</code>, <code>accordion-trigger</code>, <code
        >accordion-trigger-icon</code
      >, and <code>accordion-content</code>. Items have <code>data-open</code>
      and <code>data-disabled</code>; triggers have <code>data-panel-open</code>
      and <code>data-variant</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Each trigger is a button inside a heading, with <code>aria-expanded</code>
      and <code>aria-controls</code>, and each panel is a region named by its
      trigger. Tab and Shift+Tab move between triggers and into open content,
      Enter and Space toggle a section, and disabled triggers are skipped.
    </p>
    <p>
      The chevron turns over 120ms and content grows over 180ms. Both stop when
      reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Accordion uses <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>,
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code
        >--sprout-radius-control</code
      >, <code>--sprout-text-sm</code>, <code>--sprout-motion-fast</code>,
      <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code>, and <code>--sprout-motion-ease</code
      >, so it follows light, dark, and the TulipFarm theme.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
